Account Lock Investigation 

--Account Status
select username, account_status from dba_users where account_status like '%LOCKED%';
select username, account_status from dba_users where account_status like '%EXPIRED%';


If user account is in LOCKED(TIMED) status due to multiple failed login attempts.

--Common Return Codes:

Return Code	   >>        Description
0	             >>     Login Successful
1017	         >>   Invalid Username/Password
28000          >>     	Account Locked

--Audit Query – All Failed Login Attempts
SELECT event_timestamp,
       dbusername,
       userhost,
       return_code
FROM unified_audit_trail
WHERE return_code <> 0
  AND dbusername = 'B1'
ORDER BY event_timestamp DESC;


--Audit Query – Failed Login Attempts Within a Specific Time Range
SELECT *
FROM unified_audit_trail
WHERE dbusername = 'B1'
  AND event_timestamp >= TIMESTAMP '2026-06-10 00:00:00'
  AND event_timestamp <  TIMESTAMP '2026-06-11 12:00:00'
ORDER BY event_timestamp DESC;

Findings:
The account entered LOCKED(TIMED) status after exceeding the allowed number of failed login attempts defined in the user's profile.

Audit records can be reviewed in UNIFIED_AUDIT_TRAIL to identify:
->Failed login timestamps
->Source host (USERHOST)
->Return codes associated with each login attempt
